Ed

I had close my session, try again, and now it does save the etas in the object, no clear what is the difference. When I included the eta in monitor blavaan doesnt present the summary, but it does present the fitmeasures and I can export the posterior draws from the external$mcmcout$mcmc object.

This is a minor inconvenience

Thanks

dat <- read.csv("pos_neg.csv")
head(dat)

################################################################################
mod51 <- 'Positive =~ great + cheerful + happy
          Negative =~ sad + down + unhappy
'
fit51 <-  bcfa(mod51, data=dat, std.lv <http://std.lv>=T,
n.chains = 3, burnin=5000,
            sample=2000,

jagextra = list(monitor="eta"))

summary(fit51, standardized=T,rsquare=T,postmedian=TRUE)
Error in lavobject@Mod...@def.function(x) : unused argument (x)
fitMeasures(fit51)

ff <- fit51@external$mcmcout$mcmc
ff2 <- rbind(ff[[1]], ff[[2]], ff[[3]])
head(ff2)
dim(ff2)
colnames(ff2)

